From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Blockchain-Oracle <blockchainoracle.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 18:23:43 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wallet: persist storage through a pluggable StorageBackend

`Storage` is hard-wired to a plaintext JSON file and `WalletCore` writes
that file directly (including once per synced block). Embedders that want
to encrypt the wallet at rest, keep it in a platform keystore, or debounce
the per-block writes currently have to fork the crate.

Introduce a small `StorageBackend` trait (`load`/`save` of opaque bytes)
together with `Storage::{to_bytes, from_bytes, load_from, save_to}`. The
existing behaviour moves into the default `FileBackend`, which
`Storage::{from_path, save_to_path}` and `WalletCore` keep using, so the
on-disk format, error messages and save cadence are unchanged.

`WalletCore` gains `new_with_storage_backend` and `set_storage_backend`;
every save, including the per-block save during sync, goes through the
configured backend.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
